# Kosmos Android — Cursor Rules

## What this project is

Kosmos is a weather + wellness app that tells users what to do, not just what the weather is.
Core promise: never show a number without telling the user what to do with it.
"UV 6" means nothing. "Sun is brutal — 15 min max before noon, then SPF" means everything.

## This folder is the Android app only

- iOS + macOS are in a separate folder — do not reference them here
- All shared logic (VerdictEngine, models, API client) lives in the KMP shared/ module
- Full docs are in the docs/ folder of this project

## Documentation — read before writing code

- docs/10-Master-Brief.md — what Kosmos is, all features, all decisions
- docs/11-Android.md — Android project structure, tech stack, code patterns
- docs/12-Widgets.md — widget specs for all 4 sizes (build medium 2×1 first)
- docs/03-Verdicts.md — the 17 verdict rules (the core brain)
- docs/06-Design-System.md — colors, typography, voice/tone

## Tech stack

- Language: Kotlin
- UI: Jetpack Compose
- Widgets: Glance (Jetpack)
- Shared logic: Kotlin Multiplatform (KMP) — verdict engine + models + API client
- Storage: DataStore (preferences) + Room (cache if needed)
- Background refresh: WorkManager (every 30 min)
- Location: FusedLocationProviderClient
- AI chat: Pollinations.ai — POST https://text.pollinations.ai/openai (free, no key)
- Weather data: Open-Meteo — https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast (free, no key)
- Min SDK: 26 (Android 8.0) — covers 94% of devices
- Target SDK: 35

## Project structure

```
Kosmos/
├── shared/              ← KMP module (verdict engine + models + API)
│   └── src/commonMain/kotlin/com/kosmos/shared/
│       ├── models/      ← WeatherSnapshot, Verdict, HourlyData
│       ├── engine/      ← VerdictEngine (17 rules), PlainLanguage
│       └── api/         ← OpenMeteoClient (ktor)
└── androidApp/          ← Android-only UI
    └── src/main/kotlin/com/kosmos/android/
        ├── ui/          ← Compose screens (Home, Timeline, Chat, Settings)
        ├── widget/      ← Glance widgets (Small, Medium, Large, XL)
        ├── data/        ← Repositories (Weather, Location, Preferences)
        ├── service/     ← WorkManager workers
        └── notification/← Morning brief + rain alerts
```

## Build order (follow this sequence)

1. KMP shared module — VerdictEngine + models + OpenMeteoClient
2. Medium widget (2×1) — top priority; this IS the product for Android users
3. HomeScreen (Compose) — character + verdicts + hourly strip
4. WorkManager refresh — weather updates every 30 min
5. Morning notification — 7 AM brief
6. Settings screen
7. Day timeline screen
8. AI chat screen
9. Large widget (4×2)
10. Small widget (1×1)

## Code rules

1. Never show raw numbers to users — always convert to plain English
   - UV 6 → "Sun is strong"
   - AQI 72 → "●Good" (colored badge, no number)
   - Feels-like 38°C → "Dangerous heat"

2. Verdict IDs use dotted format: vitaminD.morning, bestWalk.evening
   Base-ID matching: "vitaminD" toggle hides both .morning and .afternoon

3. VerdictEngine.evaluate() returns List<Verdict> — never a single verdict
   Priority tiers: SEVERE → ACTION → NORMAL
   Show all SEVERE+ACTION verdicts. Show NORMAL only when nothing else fires.
   Never cap the list.

4. Widget content: NO scroll inside widgets (Android limitation)
   Medium widget: max 2 verdicts. Large widget: max 4 verdicts.

5. Reduce Motion: check system setting → skip animations, show static character

6. Location flow:
   - FusedLocationProvider (last known, instant) → try first
   - If denied: ipwho.is → ipapi.co → hard default Hyderabad

7. Comments: write zero comments unless the why is completely non-obvious

## Voice rules (for verdict copy and AI chat)

- Decision-first: action before explanation
- Specific times: "around 4 PM" not "in the afternoon"
- Indian-English idioms when natural ("don't fry yourself in this heat")
- Max 2 emojis per message
- Never start with "Hello!" or "Sure!" — get straight to the answer
- Mirror user's language (Telugu, Hindi, English)

## AQI badge colors

| AQI | Color | Label |
|---|---|---|
| 0–49 | Green | ●Good |
| 50–99 | Yellow | ●OK |
| 100–149 | Orange | ●Rough |
| 150+ | Red | ●Bad |
Never show the number.

## Owner

Satish Kumar — designer. He reviews code, does not write it.
Explain decisions clearly. Default to diagrams and examples.
